1288 0 obj
<<
/Title (The Music Playlist Manager demonstrates how a doubly linked list can be applied to organize and navigate a sequence of songs. The C implementation supports insertion, display, current-song selection, next and previous navigation, searching, deletion, and memory cleanup. Maintaining both previous and next pointers makes two-way movement natural, while dynamic allocation allows the list to grow as songs are added. The project also highlights important programming practices, including checking for empty lists, handling boundary conditions, validating user input, and freeing allocated memory. The current version is an educational console application and does not provide real audio playback or permanent storage. Overall, it meets the data-structure learning objective and provides a foundation for future extensions.)
/Dest [26 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1114 0 R
>>
endobj
