1696 0 obj
<<
/Title (The Music Playlist Manager is a menu-driven application developed in the C programming language to organize and navigate a collection of songs using a doubly linked list. In a basic playlist, users need to add songs, remove songs, view the complete list, and move between tracks in both forward and backward directions. A simple array-based list may require shifting elements after deletion and has a fixed capacity when statically allocated. This project uses dynamically allocated nodes so that the playlist can grow or shrink during execution, subject to available memory. Each node stores a song title and pointers to both the previous and next nodes. These two links make it possible to move to the next song and return to the previous song efficiently. The application provides options to add a song at the end, display the playlist, play or select a song, move to the next or previous song, search by title, delete a song, and exit safely. The program also demonstrates memory management through dynamic allocation and deallocation. The project is intended as an educational implementation of linked-list operations rather than a real audio player; it manages song information and simulated playback navigation, but does not decode or play audio files. The design is modular, with separate functions for common operations, and can be compiled using a standard C compiler. It demonstrates how a data structure can be applied to a familiar real-world task while reinforcing pointers, structures, functions, loops, and memory management.)
/Dest [16 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1684 0 R
/Next 1697 0 R
>>
endobj
